    {
      "role": "tool",
      "state": "{'type': 'text', 'text': \"<h1>Cyber Monday sales to hit $14 billion, fueled by AI, Adobe forecasts</h1>\\n<p class='meta'>Source: Yahoo | Date: 2025-12-01 11:02 | Symbol: WMT</p>\\n<p>STORY: U.S. consumers are expected to spend more than $14 billion on Cyber Monday, building on strong Black Friday momentum.:: FileThat's according to Adobe Analytics, which said AI-powered shopping tools should help boost Cyber Monday sales by 6.3% from a year earlier.Adobe Analytics tracks 1 trillion visits by shoppers to online retail websites.Cyber Monday is traditionally seen as the country's biggest online shopping day, and marks the culmination of the Thanksgiving shopping weekend.Black Friday kicked off the weekend with a record $11.8 billion in online sales, according to Adobe, as consumers switched to chatbots to compare prices amid concerns about tariff-driven price hikes.U.S. retailers have also doubled down on AI tools to lure shoppers.Adobe expects AI-driven traffic to retail sites to rise by 670% compared to last year, when AI tools like Walmart's Sparky or Amazon's Rufus had not yet been launched.</p>\\n<p>According to Yahoo, cyber monday sales to hit $14 billion, fueled by ai, adobe forecasts. \\n                        This development has significant implications for investors tracking \\n                        WMT.</p>\\n<p>Market analysts are closely monitoring this situation as it could impact \\n                        trading strategies in the coming weeks. Investors are advised to review \\n                        their positions and consider the broader market context.</p>\\n<p>STORY: U.S. consumers are expected to spend more than $14 billion on Cyber Monday, building on strong Black Friday momentum.:: FileThat's according to Adobe Analytics, which said AI-powered shopping tools should help boost Cyber Monday sales by 6.3% from a year earlier.Adobe Analytics tracks 1 trillion visits by shoppers to online retail websites.Cyber Monday is traditionally seen as the country's biggest online shopping day, and marks the culmination of the Thanksgiving shopping weekend.Black Friday kicked off the weekend with a record $11.8 billion in online sales, according to Adobe, as consumers switched to chatbots to compare prices amid concerns about tariff-driven price hikes.U.S. retailers have also doubled down on AI tools to lure shoppers.Adobe expects AI-driven traffic to retail sites to rise by 670% compared to last year, when AI tools like Walmart's Sparky or Amazon's Rufus had not yet been launched.</p>\"}",
